 It conducts operations in Arizona, California, Colorado, Florida, Idaho, Nevada, North Carolina, Texas, and Washington. The company was formerly known as Kaufman and Broad Home Corporation and changed its name to KB Home in January 2001. KB Home was founded in 1957 and is based in Los Angeles, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert V. McGibney | CEO, President & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $2.9M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $136K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $22K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["KB Home is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $3.1B market cap on $6.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 10% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $287M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.78\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 20.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (21.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries a 35% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.35132168663678764},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $17.9M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-17872340.17},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Investors Heavily Search KB Home (KBH): Here is What You Need to Know","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/investors-heavily-search-kb-home-130003918.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795611603.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.162,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"KB Home (KBH) Rises Yet Lags Behind Market: Some Facts Worth Kn